 "notes": "Piece G5 (Golden Gate Park, east end). Box moved from the assignment's 1290,955,840,657: left +15 (off the narrow road and land strip at x 1287-1300 on the park's north-west edge), top +15 (y 955 lay on the land outline at y 965-967 near x 1320 and took in the sliver between the park line and the roads), right -20 (Stanyan St's park line and heavy borders at x 2103-2125; the park line still touches the box's right edge at about x 2109, y 966-990), bottom -16 (the park's south line at y 1608-1613 and the strip below it). Lettering fills the road and touches both its lines at: CONSERVATORY DR (x 1690-1810, y 985-1013), MIDDLE DR EAST (1425-1585, 1235-1287), MARTIN L KING (1672-1737, 1316-1462), SOUTH (1572-1650, 1486-1554), DR on South Dr (1692-1740, 1496-1512), KEZAR (1868-1943, 1482-1519), DR on Kezar Dr (2035-2064, 1404-1448), WALLER (2062-2107, 1452-1468). There the ink of the letters joins the land on both sides, so each road line along the lettering is traced as a stroke; the lettering is left unseeded (street). On MARTIN L KING the east line is thick on the diagonal, so one limit runs a line-width inside it (x 1680-1735, y 1314-1464): a 2-3 px strip there has no label. Land with doubt: the land south of Kezar Dr and Waller St (x 1840-2110, y 1475-1596) is marked open park land; the line just below the box (y about 1608) is the top of block 1264. The land east of Kezar Dr (x 2040-2110, y 1200-1450) carries the zoning letters NC-1 and a small lake outline (2080, 1385): marked open park land, letters and lake joined to it. RH-3 letters (2060-2100, 1057-1075) lie in park land. A sliver of land at the box top between the diagonal road and Conservatory Dr (x 1802-1850, y 970-978) has its own open seed. Roads read as street: the dead-end road inside the Conservatory loop (closed round end at 1715-1760, 1040-1075); the narrow road (7 px) running south from the Kezar Dr / South Dr junction (x 1829-1845, y 1550-1596); Conservatory Dr's west leg, drawn only 4-8 px wide (x 1600-1660, y 1015-1080). The pond at (1570-1655, 1165-1200) is joined to the land round it. Every unseeded island left is lettering inside a road.",
